#
# Build context for every E2E image. `context: ../..` from testing/e2e-docker/ resolves HERE, so
# this file governs config/Dockerfile, Dockerfile.foundry and Dockerfile.foundry-base alike.
#
# THERE WAS NO .dockerignore AT ALL UNTIL 2026-08-24. The context was 1.8 GB, of which ~1.7 GB was
# generated output the image can never use: 984 MB of `reports/` (auditor runs, 2 tracked files out
# of thousands), and 722 MB of node_modules across the root, src-pwa/ and codebase-mcp/. Every
# build shipped all of it to the daemon, and `test:prerelease` now has four E2E legs.
#
# EXCLUDING node_modules IS A CORRECTNESS FIX, NOT ONLY A SPEED ONE.
#
# Both Dockerfiles do `COPY package*.json` -> `RUN npm ci` -> `COPY . .`. That last COPY was
# overwriting the container's freshly installed modules with the HOST's, discarding the npm ci
# layer the Dockerfile goes to the trouble of caching. It is worse on the foundry path, whose whole
# point is that `npm ci` resolves through the Verdaccio mirror on the airgapped Dev segment: built
# from a working tree on king, the host's npmjs-sourced modules landed on top of the mirror-sourced
# ones, silently defeating the supply-chain guarantee that runner exists to provide.
#
# Nothing at runtime loses node_modules by this: 14 of the 15 compose services bind-mount
# `../..:/app`, so the host tree — including its node_modules — shadows the image anyway. The 15th
# (playwright-browser) has no `build:` at all. The foundry runner is the one that genuinely relies
# on the image, and it installs its own from Verdaccio, which is exactly what this protects.
#
# Mirrors code/.gitignore deliberately, including its reports/ exception. Anything generated there
# is generated here.

# --- dependency trees: every consumer installs or mounts its own ---
**/node_modules

# --- auditor and test output (the 984 MB) ---
reports/*
!reports/llgd-coverage-baseline.json
!reports/llgd-coverage-baseline.md
coverage/
coverage-free/
testing/e2e-docker/output/
testing/e2e-engram-docker/output/
testing/live-e2e-output/

# --- build artifacts: rebuilt in-image or supplied by the mount ---
dist/
.quasar/
src-pwa/dist/
codebase-mcp/dist/

# --- local runtime state; E2E uses VM_DATA_DIR=/tmp/e2e-data, never this ---
data/

# --- VCS and editor noise ---
.git/
.gitignore
*.swp
.DS_Store
